(d) REACH
  per swept a0 the attack reaches (1-e^-1)^3 = 0.25258 = 2^-1.985 of the available
    (W1,W2,W3) solutions -> 1.985 bits discarded by the "max representative" policy.
  measured yield 2^-15.26 per swept a0 = 0.2526 * (3/4)^32 = 2.537e-05 = 2^-15.27  [check]
  family size: v,a6,a7,a10 free = 2^128 contexts x 2^32 a0 = 2^160 seeds;
    in-family preimages available = 2^160 * (3/4)^32 = 2^146.7 ; reached = 2^144.7
    against ~2^256 preimages of the 19-round compression function: the family
    reaches 2^-111 of the space, but needs only 2^15.3 seeds per preimage, so the
    restriction costs nothing in practice.
